\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Veluws is a group of dialects of the Veluwe region in the Netherlands, with West-Veluws and Oost-Veluws as main varieties. Sources disagree on classification (Low Franconian versus Low Saxon). There is no standard Veluws spelling. Little school material was found.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No school textbooks or primers were found.
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Veluws dialect: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veluws_dialect}
\item Wikipedia, West-Veluws dialect: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West-Veluws_dialect}
\item Wikipedia, Oost-Veluws dialect: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oost-Veluws_dialect}
\item Veluws spellingslijstje (community spelling guide, ECAL): \url{https://www.ecal.nu/assets/dd6cd6d8b5/Veluws-spellingslijstje.pdf}
\item Noord-Veluws word list on mijnwoordenboek.nl (user-contributed, small): \url{https://www.mijnwoordenboek.nl/dialect/Noord-Veluws}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found beyond the word list above.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
A Barneveld dictionary by H. van de Giessen and a Gelderland dialect dictionary were mentioned in search summaries but no verified URLs were seen, so they are not listed. A curriculum would have to settle on a variety and a spelling first.
\end{document}
